				1746,
				7
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Restore simple crate and bundle identifiers\n\nRestore \"Mountain\" as the crate binary, library, and package name, and the\nTauri productName and bundle identifier, replacing the verbose development\nbuild descriptors from the prior commit. The Backup files are removed.\n\nGate the Cocoon sidecar launch on both the ExtensionHostCocoon feature flag\nand the absence of the no_node_host cfg flag, so the extension host tier\nrouting (Node vs WebWorker) is respected at boot time.\n\nInclude the task type in the task provider Options payload, fixing the\nregistration schema for Cocoon's task system.\n\nDerive Clone on ExtensionCollection to support shared access patterns in\nthe terminal environment variable mutation pipeline.\n\nAdd the zsh shell integration script to the Tauri resource bundle and\ntidy resource ordering.",
			"SHA": "279ff30481d2276785d0a819d7314527ec775fb6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:31:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1748,
				4
			],
			"Message": "build(Mountain): Differentiate development build identifiers from release\n\nRename the crate binary, library, package, Tauri productName, and bundle identifier to a verbose development build descriptor encoding the full toolchain configuration (Node 22, VS Code dependency, debug profile, esbuild compiler). This prevents the development build's binary name and macOS bundle ID from colliding with the release build, enabling side-by-side installation and testing.\n\nExpand the Tauri resource bundle to include all Sky deployment variant directories (Browser, BrowserProxy, Bundled, Electron, Favicon, Isolation, Manifest.json, Mountain) that were previously omitted, ensuring the development build can serve every editor UI target.",
			"SHA": "960cc2f2c87bbd38613db3e6da10c856b2ae0dd3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:10:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1746,
				19
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement EnvironmentVariableCollection and tier defaults\n\nAdd TerminalEnvCollection — a global registry for per-extension environment variable mutations matching VS Code's `EnvironmentVariableCollection` API (Replace/Append/Prepend/Delete/Clear/SetPersistent/SetDescription). Seven `terminal.envCollection.*` Vine notification handlers in MountainVinegRPCService dispatch Cocoon's requests to the registry via TerminalEnvCollectionDispatch. At every PTY spawn, TerminalProvider collects the inherited process env, applies all registered mutators via ApplyToEnv, and layers shell-integration vars on top, ensuring extensions like language servers see the environment they requested.\n\nAdd `tree.refresh` and `outputChannel.replace` Vine notification relays: the former forwards TreeDataProvider.onDidChangeTreeData events to Sky as `sky://tree-view/refresh`; the latter provides atomic output channel buffer replacement that avoids the visual flash of separate clear+append.\n\nExpand the tier routing infrastructure by adding compile-time defaults and Info.plist entries for 14 additional subsystems (Auth, Debug, Encryption, ExtensionHost, LanguageFeatures, Model, NativeHost, OutputChannel, SCM, Search, Storage, Tasks, Terminal, TreeView, WebSocket) and extending LandFixTier::LogResolvedTiers to emit all 16 tier values at boot for full routing observability.\n\nTidy formatting across AppLifecycle, Entry, RunGit, Reload, mod.rs, CocoonManagement, Dispatcher, build.rs, and bash.sh with no semantic changes.",
			"SHA": "abba8a235310b01bca76aa32de8fe2de37a9a9af"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T13:49:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1742,
				8
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add per-subsystem tier routing and reload-safe panels\n\nIntroduce the tier routing framework that allows each IPC subsystem to be dispatched to either Mountain-native or Cocoon Node.js at compile time (via build.rs EmitTierDefaults) or at runtime (via env var overrides). Routing constants for Terminal, SCM, Debug, LanguageFeatures, Search, OutputChannel, NativeHost, TreeView, Storage, Model, Tasks, Auth, Encryption, ExtensionHost, and WebSocket are baked at build time; the `tier_routes_to_node` helper in mod.rs evaluates the tier and forwards matching commands to Cocoon's gRPC surface. Storage and SCM commands gain tier-gated arms first.\n\nImplement webview panel state persistence across `nativeHost:reload`: before the renderer reload, ask Cocoon to serialize all registered webview panels via `ExtHostWebviewPanels$serializeAllWebviewPanels` and store the snapshot in global storage under `__webview_panel_state__`. After Cocoon restarts and extensions re-activate, deserialize each panel entry via `ExtHostWebviewPanels$deserializeWebviewPanel` and clear the cache to prevent double-restore on subsequent reloads.\n\nAdd optional Mist WebSocket transport in Entry.rs: when `TierWebSocket=Mist`, a localhost JSON-RPC WebSocket binds on port 5051 for high-frequency IPC (storage updates, decorations, model changes) that bypasses the Tauri-invoke + gRPC double hop. The secret and port are exposed via environment variables for Cocoon/Sky workbench configuration consumption.\n\nApply a 30-second wall-clock timeout to git subprocess execution (RunGit.rs) so a hung git process — stalled on a credential prompt, index lock, or unresponsive network mount — releases the Mountain effect slot via the registry-aware PID killer rather than blocking indefinitely.\n\nAdd crash-safe memento hydration at boot (AppLifecycle.rs): the `MementoLoader` reads global.json, quarantines corrupted files to `.corrupted.<ts>` siblings, and populates the in-memory map from an empty baseline so a partial write from a prior crash doesn't panic the boot path.\n\nFix a minor formatting issue in bash shell integration (`2> /dev/null` to `2>/dev/null`).",
			"SHA": "db5e7784a51c6f267aa6a9c90624ad8346577df2"
		}
	],
